If your requirement strictly implies that *all* logic should be recursive (including the primality test), you can rewrite the `IsPrime` function recursively as well. Here is how that alternative looks:

```csharp
// Fully recursive IsPrime helper
static bool IsPrimeRecursive(int num, int divisor = 2)
{
    // Base cases for primality
    if (num <= 1) return false;
    if (divisor * divisor > num) return true; // No factors found up to sqrt(num)
    if (num % divisor == 0) return false;     // Factor found

